       { Id: 'm-flashback', Name: 'Recall a Flashback', Kind: 'Adventure', VirtueId: null, Description: "At any point a Hero can Recall a Flashback to take an action in the past that has relevance to their current situation — the action you want to take must make sense to have happened. Recalling a Flashback gives you Strain without Resist; the amount you take reflects the severity of the action you “took” in the past: 1 Strain for any ordinary action you could have easily done, 2 Strain for an action with the possibility of complication or some unlikely opportunity, 3 Strain for an intricate or detailed action or set of actions that involved specific opportunities or circumstances. If the action you take in the past would call for a Move, you still roll for that Move and consequences happen accordingly. You can not Recall a Flashback to “undo” a consequence or something that has already occurred.", Results: { Tier3: { Description: "No roll of its own — triggers whichever Move applies to the recalled action.", Options: [], ChooseCount: 0 }, Tier2: { Description: '—', Options: [], ChooseCount: 0 }, Tier1: { Description: '—', Options: [], ChooseCount: 0 } } },
